ium in los angeles  stretched for miles monday as cases  across california continue to spike  governor gavin newsom warned that he may  institute lockdowns in the hardest hit  counties  to try and slow down the spread you can  see in mid-december california  the icu beds will be at 112 capacity  you know despite an accelerating crisis  many americans are still resisting  basic efforts to control the virus i'll  resist  and i'm not the only one who will resist  take rapid city south dakota last night  residents debated implementing a  stricter  mask ordinance not a mass mandate after  that state  led the nation in coronavirus deaths per  capita  this month it's just a mask wear it this  is a public health crisis  i don't know what else to say the  measure passed nine to one but some  businesses can opt out  and houses of worship are exempt in  other parts of south dakota some local  leaders are taking no chances  this is a mandatory mask checkpoint set  up by the cheyenne river reservation  one in every four tests here is coming  back positive to slow the spread the  reservation's largest city was placed  on a 10-day lockdown tribal chairman  harold fraser  says the reservation has only eight  hospital beds for the twelve  thousand people that live there and if  you wanna get to the nearest icu  you've gotta drive three hours away our  main priority is to save our people  and just we know that if there is a  vaccine it's going to be a long time  come we as indian people  we're always at the back of the bus on  whatever it is  so i guess we'll just have to wait and  see it  look the chairman told us those  checkpoints are not just for checking  for mass they're for contact tracing  where are you going and when are you  coming back because a lot of native  americans are getting ill  when they leave the reservation to go  shopping for food and they come back  after being in contact with someone the  outside who is infected with the virus  one more thing before we go the